fit from  their transformers project the producers  had to work out the name and design of  the transformers well before filming  began in order for the toy giant to go  into pre-production as a result the  movie ended up featuring autobots and  decepticons which never made an  appearance in the transformers comics  the experienced star wars crew at  industrial light and magic was tasked  with bringing the robots to life on the  computer the transformers were so  detailed and complex that it took  islam's animators 38 hours to fit them  into a single frame of the film after  black hawk down and hulk transformers  was also just the third film in the 21st  century to use footage from the us air  force the film was shot at the holloman  air force base and the white sands  missile range it was well worth it as  the movie grossed more than 700 million  us dollars thus paving the way for the  big franchise in addition to stars like  shia labeouf megan fox and joshua ml  peter cullen was cast as the voice actor  for optimus prime he had already dubbed  the leader of the autobots in the  animated series from the 80s and 90s  but what plot did the creators come up  with for the big screen appearance first  let's have a brief overview of the  history of the planet cybertron which  was home to a race of intelligent  machine creatures with the ability to  transform their bodies into other forms  once optimus prime and megatron ruled  the planet together however megatron  wanted to rule over the entire universe  as a result there was a battle between  the autobots and the decepticons  megatron was after the all spark a  cube-shaped artifact that had once given  life for the machines on cybertron the  autobots knew they had no chance of  winning so they launched the old spark  into space it landed on earth as did  some autobots and decepticons years  later young samwit wiki finally gets his  own car from his parents with this car  he wants to impress michaela a teenage  girl from a school even though he's not  completely satisfied with it at first he  is so astonished his car is in fact an  alien named bumblebee who has long been  hiding on earth it turns out that the  location of the old spark is burned into  the glasses of sam's great-grandfather  100 years ago he had found both the  all-spark and megatron in the eyes  bumblebee notifies his audubon allies  but not only they learn of sam's fine so  do the decepticons thus a battle against  the clock begins with sam and his  beloved mikhail at the center of it all  it becomes especially dangerous for  everyone when megatron awakens from his  hibernation and the decepticons present  themselves to humans for the first time  in millennia  at the time the film had everything a  successful action movie needed cars  robots explosions and of course a bit of  bare skin presented here by megan fox  but what also stands out is the  heroization of the used military this  was not well received by the press given  that the crimes of the iraq war were  slowly but surely being dealt with  during this time worth mentioning is the  final battle in the fictional place  mission city in which the military  fights together with the autobots such  scenes are consistently backed with  heroic music and lots of bursts in spite  of heavy criticism from the press in the  second part also in the final battle in  the desert the creators went the extra  mile within a few minutes the military  manages to attack the decepticons on  international soil with air and naval  units and land forces again of course  with dramatic music and lots of  explosions a scenery which at that time  caused us to get goosebumps and which  conveyed the feeling that america is  strong and ready at all times it's easy  to forget that reality looks a little  different transformers therefore  naturally offered a flawless and  entertaining distraction from everyday  life and thus perhaps exactly what the  audience wanted but the glorification of 